A||N||5||Fiero5||A Fiero night before Christmas||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero5||12-24-2001||12:53 PM||||'Twas the night before Christmas, and though it was a bit windy,<BR>Not a Fiero was stirring, not even an Indy;<BR>The Formula rims were stored in the garage with care,<BR>In hopes that a new pair of rubber soon would be there;<P>The Fieros were nestled all snug under their car covers,<BR>While visions of new Mr. Mikes seats danced in the heads of Fiero lovers;<BR>And mamma in her MAFOA night shirt, and I in my NEFA ball cap,<BR>Had just settled down for a nice Christmas eve nap,<P>When out in the driveway there arose such a clatter,<BR>I sprang from my Nascar bed to see what was the matter.<BR>Away to the window I flew like a flash,<BR>Tore up the new curtains as I tried to lift up the sash. <BR>The moon on the puddles of the new-fallen rain<BR>Gave me a night light to see any objects that came,<BR>When, what roared it's engine scaring our poor cat,<BR>But a nice red Fiero, a 4 banger at that,<P>With a beautiful young woman, sporting red flowing hair she tossed,<BR>I knew in a moment that she had to be lost.<BR>More rapid than beagles that are not that tame',<BR>She whistled, and shouted, and called my Fieros by name; <BR>"Now, Fiero1! now, Fiero2! now, Fiero3 and 4!<BR>On, Fiero5! on Fiero6! on, 7, 8 and so on!<BR>To the top of the driveway! up next to the garage wall!<BR>Now drive away! drive away! drive away all!"<P>As all my Fieros roared to life and headed for the sky, like they were caught up in a wild hurricane making them all fly,<BR>When they reached their zenith, up into the sky,<BR>So past the house-top they went making me wonder why,<BR>With the red Fiero full of toys, and that red haired beauty too. <BR>She drove up with a poof, in a twinkling, I heard her on the roof?<BR>The roaring and squeeling of a rear tire, told me she must be a veteran driver.<BR>As I drew in my hand, and was turning around,<BR>Down the chimney she came with wrapped packages in a bound.<P>The gifts were dressed all in color, and we tore the paper from all of them,<BR>And as we opened each one, we saw some from Kick Hill, Dickman and IRM;<P>Her eyes -- how they twinkled! her dimples how merry!<BR>Her cheeks were like roses, her nose like a cherry!<BR>Her pouty little mouth was drawn up like a bow,<BR>And the fur coat around her was as white as the snow;<P>The stump of a popsickle she held tight in her teeth,<BR>And she pointed her approval to our lovely little wreath;<BR>She had a beautiful face and a flat sexy belly,<BR>She then went and fixed herself some peanut butter and jelly.<P>She was a vision allright, a right beautiful thing to see,<BR>And I drooled when I saw her, as my wife then went and slapped me;<BR>A wink of her eye and a twist of her hips,<BR>Soon made me want to lick my lips;<P>She spoke not a word,  and then turned with a jerk,<BR>And laying a finger aside of her nose,<BR>Then giving a nod, up my chimney she rose;<P>She sprang to her car, to my Fieros she gave a whistle,<BR>And they all came back, washed,  waxed and without even a bristle.<BR>But I heard her exclaim, as she drove out of sight,<BR>"HAPPY CHRISTMAS TO ALL, AND TO ALL A GOOD-NIGHT!"<P>Edited for spelling <p>[This message has been edited by Fiero5 (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
